### E. Wazuh Indexer

The Wazuh Indexer stores and indexes security alerts.

The Python collector communicates with the Indexer API to retrieve alert records.

### F. Python Alert Collector

The alert collector retrieves alerts from the Wazuh Indexer through its REST API.

It supports:

- Collecting the latest alerts.
- Filtering alerts by Wazuh Rule ID.
- Extracting relevant alert fields.
- Saving the collected data as JSON.

### G. Incident Processor

The incident processor transforms collected alerts into an incident-oriented data structure.

It supports the preparation of alerts for investigation by the AI analyzer.

### H. AI Analyzer

The AI analyzer provides the analyst-controlled investigation interface.

It allows the analyst to:

- Specify a Wazuh Rule ID.
- View matching incidents.
- Investigate one alert individually.
- Select multiple alerts for combined investigation.
- Submit selected evidence to the AI model.

### I. FreeLLMAPI and GPT-OSS 120B

FreeLLMAPI provides the unified API interface used by the project.

The configured Groq provider supplies access to GPT-OSS 120B.

The model receives selected security evidence and produces an investigation report.

### J. Investigation Storage

Generated investigation reports are stored locally in:

```text
logs/ai_analysis.json
```

