# 7. AI Investigation Engine

## 7.1 Model Integration

The project uses GPT-OSS 120B through the following architecture:

```text
Python AI Analyzer
        |
        v
   FreeLLMAPI
        |
        v
   Groq Provider
        |
        v
  GPT-OSS 120B
        |
        v
AI Investigation Report
```

The configured API base URL is:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:3001/v1
```

The model identifier is:

```text
gpt-oss-120b
```

The API integration uses an OpenAI-compatible chat completions interface.

## 7.2 Investigation Report Structure

The AI analyzer is designed to generate reports containing:

1. Executive Summary
2. Confirmed Evidence
3. Technical Interpretation
4. Potential Threat Scenarios
5. MITRE ATT&CK Mapping
6. False Positive Assessment
7. Recommended Investigation Steps
8. Confidence Assessment
9. Final Verdict

## 7.3 AI Analysis Requirements

The AI investigation engine should follow these principles:

- Do not invent events or evidence.
- Separate confirmed facts from hypotheses.
- Do not claim to have inspected systems or files that were not supplied.
- Treat MITRE ATT&CK mappings as evidence-based assessments.
- Identify missing information.
- Distinguish suspicious activity from confirmed malicious activity.
- Recommend additional investigation where evidence is insufficient.

The AI model provides investigative assistance, not definitive proof of compromise.

